  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Exploring Fonts\r\n\r\nNotice that there is a new section of our webpage called `<style>`. This defines the rules for how the webpage should look.\r\n\r\n> **Note:** The `<link>` tag at the top of the HTML loads fonts from <a href=\"https://fonts.google.com/?preview.text=These%20are%20google%20fonts!&lang=en_Latn\" target=\"_blank\">Google Fonts</a>. You can tell AI Tutor to use a Google Font by name.\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n1. Ask AI Tutor to explain how `font-family` work in CSS.\r\n2. Ask AI Tutor to update the paragraph text this page with a different style.\r\n   - Use the property name in your prompt (e.g., *\"Set the `font-family` to a Google font like...\"*).\r\n\r\nOnce you've styled the page, click **Continue**.",
